<title>UK: Rolls Royce gets $500 mln Trent 700 order.</title>
<headline>Rolls Royce gets $500 mln Trent 700 order.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Rolls Royce Plc said on Monday it had received a $500 million order for Trent 700 engines to power Emirates airline's fleet of Airbus Industrie A330-200 aircraft.  </p>
<p>The Dubai-based airline ordered 16 of the aircraft from Airbus, with options on another seven jetliners, Rolls Royce said in a statement. Deliveries begin in January 1999.</p>
<p>Rolls Royce said the order made Emirates one of the UK's biggest airline customers, including its previous order for Trent 800 engines for its seven Boeing Co 777 aircraft.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
